lead:
Every binary file gets a value-free entropy profile: whole-file 4 KiB block statistics, plus 16 fixed segments. STDF V4 becomes its own family. squalify:
- reads the endianness from FAR;
- walks every record header;
- counts record types and records their first-occurrence order;
- detects truncation;
- builds a **test catalog** (test number, kind, name and occurrences) from PTR, MPR, FTR and TSR. The catalog is always included, up to a cap.

sections.body:
Goal: the v1 formats.

Owner decision (2026-10-13): walk the records and build the test catalog. Test names act like column headers, so they are always included.

DataBall's `StdfHandler` only matches the extension and its `Parse` throws (`DataBall/src/DataBall.Handlers/StdfHandler.cs:11-34`), so there is nothing to reuse. The layouts come from pystdf (`pystdf/V4.py`, `pystdf/IO.py`), because the Teradyne PDF could not be reached during the spec pass:
- the header is REC_LEN U2 (payload length only) + REC_TYP U1 + REC_SUB U1;
- FAR is (0, 10), with CPU_TYPE U1 and STDF_VER U1, and CPU_TYPE 2 means little-endian;
- PTR (15, 10): TEST_NUM U4, HEAD U1, SITE U1, TEST_FLG B1, PARM_FLG B1, RESULT R4, TEST_TXT Cn;
- MPR (15, 15): TEST_NUM, HEAD, SITE, TEST_FLG, PARM_FLG, RTN_ICNT U2, RSLT_CNT U2, RTN_STAT N1×j, RTN_RSLT R4×k, TEST_TXT;
- FTR (15, 20): TEST_TXT comes after the fixed fields, the RTN and PGM arrays, FAIL_PIN Dn, VECT_NAM, TIME_SET and OP_CODE;
- TSR (10, 30): HEAD, SITE, TEST_TYP C1, TEST_NUM U4, EXEC_CNT, FAIL_CNT, ALRM_CNT, TEST_NAM Cn;
- trailing fields may be missing from a short record.
